{
  "about": "The conformance vectors for docs/INTERCHANGE.md. Each file is replayed as `node packages/verify/dist/cli.js replay <file>`, followed by the vector's args when it has any; each entry of also is a further run of the same file with its own args. engine_exit and engine_says are what that command must give (exit code; a phrase in its first stderr line). binding is what a binding-only verifier must answer: holds (exit 2), fails (exit 1) or refused (exit 3). computed_* are recomputed from the bundle's own inputs and identity parts; recorded_* are what the verdict carries. sha256 is the hash of the vector file's bytes: a checkout that changes them (line endings, a byte-order mark) no longer tests what it says. The pack is listed in conformance/SPEC.md.",
  "engine_version_when_written": "0.6.0",
